00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:47.690
Fat chance you earned it, though.

00:02:47.690 --> 00:02:50.860
Anyway. It's hopeless.
Just die. That's all.

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:54.700
I obtained the title "The Best Amicide."

00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:56.780
You aren't lying, are you?

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:59.700
Enter the words of the promise.

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:01.360
Enter the words

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:05.080
Why is this locked behind a password?

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:08.660
We are best friends forever

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:10.080
We are best friends forever

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:13.010
Not only were you haunted by a ghost,

00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:15.800
but you also escaped your
crazed childhood friend.

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:17.760
Not bad, I must say.

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:23.680
Some people could take a decade
and never figure those words out.

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:24.890
Very well.

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:28.230
I'll tell you the trick to Kiwame Quest.

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:30.060
The trick?

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:35.110
Your chance of survival might
just go from 0.1% to about 0.5%.

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:37.780
That's practically no change!

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:40.370
But first, you must endure
the five days of training.

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:43.160
Endure until the second wave
of the goblin assault.

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:47.330
But be warned, depending on the player,

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:48.870
it will break you.

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:50.500
For real?

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:53.460
This game really is extreme.

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:56.170
For you garbage players it will be tough,

00:03:56.170 --> 00:04:00.050
but a failure who can't overcome
this will never succeed in life.

00:04:00.050 --> 00:04:02.850
Dig deep, even if you have to fake it.

00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:06.890
True, the goblin assault is
a hellish event with SS-difficulty.

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:11.610
But once you clear it,
you'll encounter the true mystery of Ted.

00:04:11.610 --> 00:04:14.480
Try to keep your eyes open,

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:16.490
and <i>think</i>.

00:04:16.490 --> 00:04:21.990
I wrote that the chance of survival
is 0.1%, but despite that I cleared it.

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:27.830
In other words, you're on the
razor's edge, but it's not impossible.

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:31.080
Got that, worm?

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:38.800
His tone was nasty as ever,

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:40.220
but it was like...

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:44.720
Like he was saying,
"Can you do it? I did. Now it's your turn."

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:47.980
That's the feeling I got.

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:50.060
I still have my second custard cup,

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:52.480
but I've lost my appetite.

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:57.230
I don't want to brick my console,
nor do I have the money for a new one.

00:04:57.230 --> 00:05:01.490
It would be reasonable to
quit KQ at this point, but...

00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:10.250
What? You're disturbing me.

00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:12.210
Here. For you.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:16.340
C-Custard? Why?

00:05:16.340 --> 00:05:19.470
I'm about to play
that full-dive RPG again.

00:05:19.470 --> 00:05:21.470
What? You didn't sell it?

00:05:21.470 --> 00:05:22.630
I tried to.

00:05:22.630 --> 00:05:24.600
But... I decided not to.

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:26.970
Why? You said it was a shitty game.

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:30.680
Yeah. It couldn't be shittier.
It's the epitome of a shitty game.

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:32.140
But...

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:35.560
You threw in the towel on
running and took up full-dive RPGs,

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:38.150
and to top it off you even abandon that!

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:41.450
You're just pathetic!

00:05:41.450 --> 00:05:45.410
I decided to at least get
to a good ending point.

00:05:45.410 --> 00:05:48.790
You came just to tell me <i>that</i>?

00:05:48.790 --> 00:05:51.500
School is off for several days.

00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:53.500
So, I'd like to play the whole time.

00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:55.830
So I also wanted to warn you.

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:57.840
Why tell me this?

00:05:57.840 --> 00:06:00.880
Kaede, I think I'll scream again tonight.

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:03.380
Obviously I'll try not to, but I'll fail.

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:04.930
No doubt I'll scream.

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:08.970
Wh-What's going on here?
Are you messing with--

00:06:08.970 --> 00:06:10.890
Kaede.

00:06:10.890 --> 00:06:12.850
It's just like you said.

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:18.190
I feel like, ever since I quit running,
I've been running away from things.

00:06:19.820 --> 00:06:21.610
I'll probably end up bothering you.

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:22.990
But,

00:06:22.990 --> 00:06:25.610
I want to see something through.

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:27.240
Please let me.

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:34.540
Oh, whatever! Leave me alone.

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:39.460
I'm sorry, Kaede.

00:06:41.550 --> 00:06:43.090
Are you ready now?

00:06:43.090 --> 00:06:43.920
Yeah!

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:45.840
To Queen Govern's mansion then.

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:47.220
Let's go!

00:06:50.470 --> 00:06:51.850
I saw.

00:06:51.850 --> 00:06:56.020
In the walkthrough. The stuff
about 0.1% chance of survival.

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:57.230
Oh.

00:06:57.230 --> 00:07:01.150
You should've checked the
walkthrough first! Nincompoop.

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:03.150
Nothing I can do now.

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:07.320
Anyway, we need to
make it through the training.

00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:09.070
Five days...

00:07:09.070 --> 00:07:12.450
Just what happens?
He said it could break me.

00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:14.870
No idea.

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:20.670
New recruits to the Guard
sleep at the training grounds.

00:07:20.670 --> 00:07:23.840
But first we greet Queen Govern.

00:07:23.840 --> 00:07:25.840
I see.

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:30.930
The cries of someone being tortured again.

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:33.560
That's disturbing.

00:07:36.350 --> 00:07:38.690
I appreciate your enlistment.

00:07:38.690 --> 00:07:43.070
I am Govern. I administer this city.

00:07:43.070 --> 00:07:44.990
P-Pleased to meet you.

00:07:44.990 --> 00:07:49.870
Not what I imagined
from the name "Govern"...

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:54.700
Huh?

00:07:56.500 --> 00:07:58.580
Guards are the treasure of the city.

00:07:58.580 --> 00:08:03.050
Please protect the people
of the city from the goblins.

00:08:03.050 --> 00:08:07.090
I will be praying for your safety.

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:11.180
That was <i>hilarious</i>!

00:08:11.180 --> 00:08:13.350
And the sound you made!

00:08:13.350 --> 00:08:16.730
You sounded like a certain
popstar breaking into a dance.

00:08:16.730 --> 00:08:21.190
Anyone would react that way
to suddenly being latched onto.

00:08:21.190 --> 00:08:26.110
Oh? Then maybe I should
test that some time.

00:08:26.110 --> 00:08:28.030
D-Don't...

00:08:28.030 --> 00:08:29.860
...do that.

00:08:31.870 --> 00:08:34.450
Here are the training grounds.

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:40.250
Everyone, I'd like to
introduce a new colleague.

00:08:40.250 --> 00:08:46.130
This is Hiro. He has temporarily
enlisted as a mercenary.

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:49.630
I-I look forward to
fighting alongside you.

00:08:49.630 --> 00:08:51.720
And we have two more.

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:55.640
There were other new recruits?

00:08:55.640 --> 00:08:59.100
This is Granada and Palù.
They are also mercs.

00:08:59.100 --> 00:08:59.980
Hey.

00:08:59.980 --> 00:09:01.310
'Sup.

00:09:01.310 --> 00:09:05.320
All of you, make our three
new recruits feel welcome.

00:09:05.320 --> 00:09:06.440
Welcome!

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:07.820
Glad to have you!

00:09:07.820 --> 00:09:11.320
Your efforts have driven the goblins back.

00:09:11.320 --> 00:09:13.780
However, the goblins may attack again.

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:15.950
Train hard and be ready!

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:17.830
Yes, sir!

00:09:17.830 --> 00:09:21.670
The goblins' target this time
seemed to be Queen Govern's mansion.

00:09:21.670 --> 00:09:26.800
Perhaps their monster instincts told them
the city would fall if the mansion falls.

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:31.970
We must protect the city
and protect Queen Govern!

00:09:31.970 --> 00:09:36.640
That is our duty as
members of the Ted City Guard!

00:09:37.930 --> 00:09:40.520
Work hard, Hiro.

00:09:41.350 --> 00:09:44.610
Huh? I thought Tesla would be training me.

00:09:44.610 --> 00:09:46.360
Hey. Thanks for joining.

00:09:46.360 --> 00:09:49.610
To start, let me show you
your lodgings. Follow me.

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:52.570
I'm Bob.

00:09:52.570 --> 00:09:56.780
I just became a Guard about a month ago,
so I'm only technically your senior.

00:09:56.780 --> 00:09:58.200
No need for formality.

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:00.370
Thanks, Bob.

00:10:01.750 --> 00:10:04.120
Nobody seemed very strong.

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:08.300
Well, you're obviously
the strongest, Granada.

00:10:08.300 --> 00:10:10.380
You mercs have pluck.

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:13.300
That's the spirit!

00:10:17.390 --> 00:10:19.850
So this is my room.

00:10:19.850 --> 00:10:22.350
Reona, you've been quiet.

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:26.560
I thought it best not to
speak during explanations.

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:29.150
I want you to focus on the game.

00:10:29.150 --> 00:10:32.280
I see. So there's a
method to your madness.

00:10:32.280 --> 00:10:35.280
Of course. I'm a first-rate game advisor!

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:37.700
And not a hint of irony.

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:41.080
Well, I'm gonna get changed now.

00:10:41.080 --> 00:10:42.700
Go ahead. I don't mind.

00:10:42.700 --> 00:10:44.460
I <i>do </i>mind!

00:10:44.460 --> 00:10:45.870
Oh, you do?

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:48.250
Not like there's anything to see, anyway.

00:10:48.250 --> 00:10:51.920
Did I just hear crude remarks?

00:10:55.220 --> 00:10:56.180
All changed?

00:10:56.180 --> 00:10:57.720
Yep. All set.

00:10:57.720 --> 00:11:01.350
Then let's head back. It's time
for some light practical training.

00:11:01.350 --> 00:11:02.720
W-With a sword?

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:04.690
Yes. And martial arts.

00:11:04.690 --> 00:11:06.980
All right! Finally, a tutorial!

00:11:06.980 --> 00:11:09.570
The game's been strangely RPG-like lately!

00:11:09.570 --> 00:11:11.440
Now, no need to be nervous!

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:15.950
Today's more like an
introduction exercise. You can relax.

00:11:15.950 --> 00:11:18.910
Hmm. What's this?

00:11:18.910 --> 00:11:20.410
Wh-What's what?

00:11:20.410 --> 00:11:25.830
You're pretty slender. Do you specialize
in covert operations or something?

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:28.130
Covert? Not really.

00:11:28.130 --> 00:11:32.130
Is that so? Well, I suppose
you'll be fine. I suppose.

00:11:32.130 --> 00:11:34.010
Right.

00:11:37.680 --> 00:11:39.720
Come at me!

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:40.680
What's wrong?

00:11:40.680 --> 00:11:41.640
Put more oomph into it!

00:11:41.640 --> 00:11:44.180
Whoops, it's already started.

00:11:44.180 --> 00:11:45.480
Oh, Instructor!

00:11:45.480 --> 00:11:49.770
New recruits Granada and Palù.
And Hiro, I presume.

00:11:49.770 --> 00:11:52.230
Wait, you?!

00:11:52.230 --> 00:11:55.820
This guy's the instructor?!

00:11:55.820 --> 00:11:58.910
I'm Amos, the Training Instructor here.

00:11:58.910 --> 00:12:00.120
You better do as I say!

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:02.030
Otherwise we'll throw you out!

00:12:02.030 --> 00:12:03.450
Especially you!

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:04.500
M-Me?

00:12:04.500 --> 00:12:07.460
Captain Tesla seems to
have taken a liking to you.

00:12:07.460 --> 00:12:09.750
But skill and ability
are what matters here!

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:12.460
There's no room for dead weight!

00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:13.710
You mean, "Yes, sir!"

00:12:13.710 --> 00:12:15.300
And where were your salutes?

00:12:15.300 --> 00:12:17.880
Yes, sir...

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:20.300
I better get things into gear.

00:12:20.300 --> 00:12:23.760
Hiro! So you became a Guard after all.

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:24.350
Huh?

00:12:24.350 --> 00:12:25.770
I'm Cathy.

00:12:25.770 --> 00:12:29.140
After the goblin attack...

00:12:31.060 --> 00:12:34.190
I was the one who took that girl home.

00:12:34.190 --> 00:12:37.110
She told me about how you saved her.

00:12:37.110 --> 00:12:40.490
Freaking Amos. He just pushed
the job on someone else.

00:12:40.490 --> 00:12:43.950
I'm glad to have a brave ally.

00:12:43.950 --> 00:12:45.700
Nice to meet you.

00:12:45.700 --> 00:12:48.620
Of course. The feeling is mutual.

00:12:48.620 --> 00:12:50.210
Hey! You two!

00:12:50.210 --> 00:12:52.330
You're supposed to be training!

00:12:52.330 --> 00:12:54.710
What makes you think you can loaf about?

00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:57.170
You know what? Fine.

00:12:57.170 --> 00:13:00.130
We'll start practical
training with you, Hiro!

00:13:04.050 --> 00:13:06.350
All right!

00:13:06.350 --> 00:13:07.720
Bring it on.

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:12.100
I was nearly killed by frenzied goblins
and a frenzied childhood friend.

00:13:12.100 --> 00:13:15.360
A wooden sword match is nothing.

00:13:23.490 --> 00:13:27.240
W-Well, now you look serious.

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:28.830
Good luck, Hiro!

00:13:28.830 --> 00:13:31.170
Let's eat together after!

00:13:31.170 --> 00:13:32.710
All right!

00:13:32.710 --> 00:13:34.170
Sh-Show some respect!

00:13:34.170 --> 00:13:36.630
C-C-Come at me!

00:13:36.630 --> 00:13:38.920
Fine. Here I come!

00:13:41.260 --> 00:13:42.760
What?

00:13:48.890 --> 00:13:51.310
S-So you're good.

00:13:51.310 --> 00:13:53.020
Shake it off, Hiro!

00:13:53.020 --> 00:13:57.230
Hiro, stay calm and watch
his movements carefully!

00:14:00.820 --> 00:14:04.320
Now that I look,
that's an amateur's stance.

00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:13.080
My hands are tingling!

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:14.210
Come on now!

00:14:14.210 --> 00:14:20.760
From your loafing
I thought you might be tough.

00:14:20.760 --> 00:14:24.260
But you're a weakling.

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:33.560
He sucks...

00:14:33.560 --> 00:14:35.650
Seriously? He's so weak!

00:14:35.650 --> 00:14:37.400
Well, look how skinny he is.

00:14:37.400 --> 00:14:40.360
A merchant could do better.
Build some muscle.

00:14:40.360 --> 00:14:43.240
So that's what Bob was concerned about.

00:14:43.240 --> 00:14:46.490
Everybody does look pretty built...

00:14:46.490 --> 00:14:48.370
Hiro, are you okay?

00:14:48.370 --> 00:14:50.910
I didn't know Amos was so strong.

00:14:50.910 --> 00:14:53.080
I mean, he's an instructor with the Guard.

00:14:53.080 --> 00:14:57.170
He wouldn't lose to a high-school
student. This isn't a manga.

00:14:57.170 --> 00:15:00.300
Sure, it's not a manga, but it <i>is </i>a game!

00:15:00.300 --> 00:15:02.550
Whoa!

00:15:07.090 --> 00:15:09.760
That all ya got, teach?

00:15:09.760 --> 00:15:13.390
Tr-Training is over for today!

00:15:13.390 --> 00:15:15.640
Ow, ow, ow.

00:15:15.640 --> 00:15:17.350
He wasn't much.

00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:19.020
You're amazing, Granada!

00:15:19.020 --> 00:15:21.020
We gained a strong ally!

00:15:21.020 --> 00:15:23.240
I bet he could beat a goblin!

00:15:23.240 --> 00:15:25.700
H-Hey, Bob.

00:15:25.700 --> 00:15:28.240
Training is over, so...

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:29.740
...shall we go?

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:35.540
Uh... actually something came up. Sorry.

00:15:35.540 --> 00:15:37.290
Hey, um...

00:15:37.290 --> 00:15:39.130
Huh?

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:42.670
It was incredible!

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:45.090
The food's good today.

00:15:50.680 --> 00:15:52.890
You've been totally ostracized.

00:15:52.890 --> 00:15:54.850
Don't say it out loud.

00:15:54.850 --> 00:15:56.980
Hiro, you look pretty out of place.

00:15:56.980 --> 00:16:01.070
This was the obvious result of a high
schooler becoming a mercenary.

00:16:01.070 --> 00:16:03.530
You should've thought more
before volunteering.

00:16:03.530 --> 00:16:06.780
It seemed like a classic video game event!

00:16:06.780 --> 00:16:08.860
Well, it's only five days!

00:16:08.860 --> 00:16:11.200
Just tough it out and it'll be over!

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:14.700
And you'll get to learn Kamui's trick!

00:16:14.700 --> 00:16:16.620
Y-You're right.

00:16:16.620 --> 00:16:19.960
It's only the first day. I don't
need Kamui making fun of me.

00:16:19.960 --> 00:16:21.880
That's the spirit, Hiro!

00:16:21.880 --> 00:16:25.210
You've been made fun of enough already!

00:16:27.550 --> 00:16:29.550
This was a tiring day.

00:16:29.550 --> 00:16:31.510
Shall we sleep until morning?

00:16:31.510 --> 00:16:33.970
Huh? Sleep inside the game?

00:16:33.970 --> 00:16:36.850
You've played full-dive
RPGs before, right?

00:16:36.850 --> 00:16:40.190
Sleeping in the game is pretty common.

00:16:40.190 --> 00:16:42.230
Well, that's true.

00:16:42.230 --> 00:16:43.730
Are you lonely? Is that it?

00:16:43.730 --> 00:16:44.940
Want me to join you?

00:16:44.940 --> 00:16:47.030
N-No thanks!

00:16:47.030 --> 00:16:49.660
Oh, too bad.

00:16:49.660 --> 00:16:52.530
J-Join me?

00:16:52.530 --> 00:16:56.200
What would've happened if I'd said yes?

00:17:00.080 --> 00:17:02.630
What? Already?!

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:08.090
Day 2

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:08.090
Day 2

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:08.470
Hiro, wake up. It's morning.

00:17:08.470 --> 00:17:11.300
G-Good morning...

00:17:11.300 --> 00:17:13.390
This groggy feeling...

00:17:13.390 --> 00:17:16.680
They're even realistic about this, too?

00:17:16.680 --> 00:17:22.150
They used cutting-edge neuroscience to
make you feel as if you'd slept for hours.

00:17:22.150 --> 00:17:25.520
Unnecessarily high tech of them.

00:17:25.520 --> 00:17:29.280
More importantly,
everyone's already training.

00:17:29.280 --> 00:17:32.570
What?! Lead with that!

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:37.910
I'm sorry I'm late!

00:17:40.210 --> 00:17:45.130
My, Granada, you've got
such talent! Yes, yes. That's it!

00:17:45.130 --> 00:17:47.590
Just keep going like that.

00:17:47.590 --> 00:17:51.720
Amos is already buttering him up.

00:17:51.720 --> 00:17:53.720
Huh? Oh, you. You're here?

00:17:53.720 --> 00:17:55.680
Of course I'm here!

00:17:55.680 --> 00:17:59.180
Hiro, I know he's frustrating,
but he's still the instructor.

00:17:59.180 --> 00:18:00.600
Let's act like it.

00:18:00.600 --> 00:18:02.560
R-Right.

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:06.190
Excuse me, Instructor Amos.
What should I do?

00:18:06.190 --> 00:18:08.070
Try practice swings.

00:18:08.070 --> 00:18:10.150
Practice swings.

00:18:10.150 --> 00:18:13.360
If I do those, will I discover
a special move or something?

00:18:13.360 --> 00:18:15.950
Don't be silly! Are you a child?

00:18:15.950 --> 00:18:17.910
But Tesla has a special move.

00:18:17.910 --> 00:18:21.830
He's a genius while you're mediocre!

00:18:21.830 --> 00:18:24.420
Why did he even recruit you?

00:18:24.420 --> 00:18:28.750
Please just teach me.
I'll practice as hard as I can.

00:18:28.750 --> 00:18:32.840
Listen here. You think a
little practice is all it takes?

00:18:32.840 --> 00:18:36.800
If it was, why the hell would
we have trained for years?

00:18:36.800 --> 00:18:39.060
Y-You have a point, sir.

00:18:39.060 --> 00:18:42.060
Besides, you're utterly hopeless.

00:18:42.060 --> 00:18:44.100
You completely lack talent for this.

00:18:44.100 --> 00:18:47.730
You're like an 80-year-old
who wants to become a dancer!

00:18:47.730 --> 00:18:49.320
Do you get it?

00:18:49.320 --> 00:18:53.110
I'm treated like a geezer?!
I'm the game's protagonist!

00:18:53.110 --> 00:18:54.990
Well, you can't say he's wrong.

00:18:54.990 --> 00:18:57.120
Why don't you do
practice swings like he says?

00:18:57.120 --> 00:18:59.870
F-Fine.

00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:08.710
I heard this guy murdered his best friend.

00:19:08.710 --> 00:19:14.590
Really? And he's allowed to join?
What if he comes for us while we sleep?

00:19:14.590 --> 00:19:20.680
No, that was all a misunderstanding.
Tesla determined it was an accident, so--

00:19:21.770 --> 00:19:24.560
Stop dragging everyone down.

00:19:24.560 --> 00:19:25.940
Huh?

00:19:25.940 --> 00:19:30.440
One weak link can make the chain fail.

00:19:30.440 --> 00:19:31.900
Get me?

00:19:31.900 --> 00:19:34.030
W-Well I uh...

00:19:35.030 --> 00:19:38.070
Hiro, you can train with me if you like.

00:19:38.070 --> 00:19:40.120
Th-Thanks!

00:19:40.120 --> 00:19:42.790
Pathetic.

00:19:42.790 --> 00:19:45.250
What's wrong? Change your mind?

00:19:45.250 --> 00:19:49.420
N-Not at all! Coming! I'll be right there!

00:19:49.420 --> 00:19:52.340
You have a friend. Reassuring, huh?

00:19:52.340 --> 00:19:54.630
It is.

00:19:54.630 --> 00:19:55.970
I'm pooped.

00:19:55.970 --> 00:19:57.380
I'm so hungry.

00:19:57.380 --> 00:19:58.510
Whad'ya think we get?

00:19:58.510 --> 00:19:59.970
Bread, like always.

00:19:59.970 --> 00:20:03.770
Use your pinky, ring finger,
and middle finger more.

00:20:03.770 --> 00:20:07.020
Your thumb and pointer
can be like support.

00:20:07.020 --> 00:20:08.270
O-Okay.

00:20:08.270 --> 00:20:13.820
Bend your right elbow slightly,
and use your left arm as solid support.

00:20:13.820 --> 00:20:15.240
L-Like this?

00:20:15.240 --> 00:20:18.410
Yeah. Looks good.

00:20:18.410 --> 00:20:21.580
"L-Like <i>this</i>?" That's you!

00:20:23.490 --> 00:20:25.290
Okay, break's over!

00:20:25.290 --> 00:20:27.620
You over there! Get moving!

00:20:27.620 --> 00:20:32.000
Oh, Granada, you're fine as you are.

00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:36.720
Thanks to Cathy I actually
managed to learn something.

00:20:38.800 --> 00:20:42.260
Day 3

00:20:38.800 --> 00:20:42.260
Day 3

00:20:39.220 --> 00:20:43.640
Today we're supposed to
learn practical techniques, but...

00:20:43.640 --> 00:20:45.350
I'm screwed.

00:20:45.350 --> 00:20:50.730
Begin the practice matches on my command!

00:20:50.730 --> 00:20:52.610
Begin!

00:20:55.230 --> 00:20:58.200
Oh, come on! This isn't practice!

00:20:58.200 --> 00:21:02.950
Forget goblins. One of those
strikes will take me out first!

00:21:02.950 --> 00:21:04.620
What's wrong, Hiro?

00:21:04.620 --> 00:21:09.460
G-Grip tightly with this finger,
then support... right arm...

00:21:09.460 --> 00:21:12.460
Wait. How did it go? Dammit!

00:21:12.460 --> 00:21:14.630
Only one option now!

00:21:16.170 --> 00:21:21.180
Go all-out! Strike with all my might!

00:21:21.180 --> 00:21:22.550
Huh?

00:21:22.550 --> 00:21:26.640
What was that wimpy attack?

00:21:26.640 --> 00:21:29.390
Match over! Winner, Granada!

00:21:29.390 --> 00:21:30.440
Nice move!

00:21:30.440 --> 00:21:32.520
Go, Granada!

00:21:34.770 --> 00:21:38.530
Just quit already.

00:21:38.530 --> 00:21:41.660
Having you here is worse than useless.

00:21:41.660 --> 00:21:46.410
If you don't wanna leave,
start paying us for the privilege.

00:21:46.410 --> 00:21:50.460
Yeah. Then you'd be worth having around.

00:22:00.550 --> 00:22:04.720
This is my life, even in a game?

00:23:45.730 --> 00:23:49.950
A Fairy's Power

00:23:46.160 --> 00:23:49.370
Episode 9: A Fairy's Power.
